# Scroll far up with the mouse wheel to exercise the real terminal
# emulator's own scrollback buffer, not just kiln's internal viewport.
# Whether kiln's fullscreen (alt-screen) mode leaves anything in the
# terminal's native scrollback at all is exactly the open question here
# (see scripts/qa/drive.py's Run.buffer()/screen() split and the
# scrollback_rows figure it records on every SHOT) — not established by
# reading source, since it depends on the terminal emulator's own alt-
# screen handling, not on kiln.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/scroll-long.yaml
@size 120x40

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE tell me the whole story
KEY enter
WAITFOR /SCROLL-BOTTOM-MARKER/ 20
SHOT bottom

SCROLL up 40
SHOT far-scrollback
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
NOTE check this SHOT's result.json scrollback_rows figure: >0 means the
NOTE terminal emulator held native scrollback behind kiln's alt-screen
NOTE frame; 0 means SCROLL up 40 only moved (or failed to move) kiln's
NOTE own viewport, with nothing beyond it to reach.
